{
  "manufacturer": "Yaskawa",
  "manufacturer_slug": "yaskawa",
  "model": "Z1000U HVAC Matrix Bypass (BACnet MS/TP)",
  "model_slug": "z1000u-bypass",
  "aliases": [
    "Z1000U Bypass",
    "Z1000U Matrix Bypass",
    "Z1D1",
    "Z1000U HVAC MATRIX Drive Bypass",
    "Z1000U low harmonic bypass",
    "SIEP YAIZ1D 01"
  ],
  "equipment_type": "Variable frequency drive with bypass (HVAC)",
  "applies_to": "Yaskawa Z1000U HVAC Matrix low-harmonic drive bypass packages (Z1D1, 208 V and 480 V) connected to BACnet MS/TP at the bypass controller.",
  "summary": "On the Z1000U Matrix bypass the BACnet MS/TP connection is made at the bypass controller (terminal TB3), which exposes drive and bypass data from one address. The list has the drive objects plus bypass I/O, bypass run/transfer/smoke-purge commands, HOA and contactor status and bypass fault flags.",
  "bacnet_transport": [
    "BACnet MS/TP"
  ],
  "firmware": null,
  "default_device_instance": 1,
  "access_inferred": false,
  "notes": [
    "Objects named Not used/Not Used (AI3-AI5, BV1, BV2, BV5, BV6, BV60, BV68, BV100) are left out. The manual prints BO10/BO11 as B010/B011.",
    "This MS/TP table matches the Z1000 Bypass list except that it uses PID names (AV3, AV19-AV21, BO4, BV23) and stops at AV33 and BI27; the later run-time and fault-code objects (AV35-AV42, BI28-BI30) are not in this table.",
    "The same manual also has a separate BACnet/IP object table for the Ethernet option (Z4 parameters); it is not included here (see the Yaskawa JOHB-SMP3 BACnet/IP list).",
    "BV72-BV79 (network digital inputs) are disabled unless Z3-12 = 1; those inputs are ORed with the physical inputs.",
    "BV42 and BV43 registers are printed as 8785H bit 8 and 8485H bit 9; they are listed as printed.",
    "Each description gives the Modbus register where the manual lists one."
  ],
  "source": {
    "title": "YASKAWA Z1000U HVAC MATRIX Drive Bypass Technical Manual (Appendix C.6, BACnet MS/TP Objects)",
    "doc_number": "SIEP YAIZ1D 01E",
    "revision_date": "2026-07",
    "url": "https://www.yaskawa.com/delegate/getAttachment?documentId=SIEPYAIZ1D01&cmd=documents&documentName=SIEPYAIZ1D01.pdf"
  },
  "integration": {
    "summary": "Wire BACnet MS/TP to TB3 on the bypass controller and set Z3-01 = 3 (BACnet), Z3-02 node, Z3-03 baud and the device instance in Z3-08/Z3-09, then cycle power. Set Z1-07 = 2 and Z1-08 = 2 so the network supplies the speed reference and run command, put the HOA in AUTO, then write BV58 and AV2. Read BV89 and BV90, and choose the comm-loss action in Z3-05/Z3-06.",
    "minimum_points": [
      {
        "ref": "BV 58",
        "name": "BYP Run Fwd CMD",
        "why": "Start/stop from the BMS (bypass)"
      },
      {
        "ref": "AV 2",
        "name": "Frequency Cmd",
        "why": "Frequency reference, units per o1-03"
      },
      {
        "ref": "BV 70",
        "name": "BYP Fault Reset CMD",
        "why": "Reset a bypass fault"
      },
      {
        "ref": "BV 89",
        "name": "BYP RUN Status",
        "why": "Running status"
      },
      {
        "ref": "BV 82",
        "name": "BYP AUTO Mode Status",
        "why": "HOA in AUTO, so BMS commands apply"
      },
      {
        "ref": "AV 10",
        "name": "Output Frequency",
        "why": "Output frequency, units per o1-03"
      },
      {
        "ref": "AV 31",
        "name": "Motor Current",
        "why": "Motor amps"
      },
      {
        "ref": "AV 13",
        "name": "Output Power",
        "why": "Drive power in kW"
      },
      {
        "ref": "BV 90",
        "name": "BYP Fault Status",
        "why": "Any active bypass fault"
      },
      {
        "ref": "AV 7",
        "name": "Fault Details",
        "why": "Bit-coded active fault flags"
      }
    ],
    "enable": "Table C.1: Z1-07 Speed Reference Select = 2 and Z1-08 Run Command Select = 2 (BACnet / serial) let the network set speed and start the unit; both default to 1 (terminals / bypass digital input). BV58/BV59 run the bypass forward/reverse, BV69 selects drive or bypass and BV67 selects AUTO. Monitoring, parameter access, fault set/reset and the multi-function inputs work at any time.",
    "heartbeat": "Z3-11 = 1 (default) enables comm-fault detection. Z3-05 sets the action when nothing is received for Z3-06 (0.0-99.9 s, default 2.0 s; 0.0 never times out): 0 ignore, 1 alarm only (default), 2 EF0 fault to the drive, 3 EF0 and open the bypass contactor K3, 4 alarm AL14 and run at the Z3-10 preset speed. Z3-13 can restore the last BACnet speed and/or run commands after a power loss (default 0 = off).",
    "remote_sensors": "AV3 PID Setpoint Cmd lets the BMS write the PID setpoint (-100 to 100 %). BV72-BV79 can act as the bypass digital inputs from the network when Z3-12 = 1.",
    "setup": [
      "Z3-01 = 3 selects BACnet (the default); Z3-02 is the MS/TP node (0-127, default 1).",
      "Z3-03 baud: default 3 = 9600 bps, up to 115200 bps; 1200-4800 bps give oPE29 with BACnet on bypass software VST800400 and later.",
      "Device instance = Z3-08 (low word) + Z3-09 (high word), in hex; default 1.",
      "Cycle power after changing Z3 settings; DIP switch S1 (or an external 120 ohm resistor) terminates the end of the line.",
      "The device object name (20 characters) is writable over BACnet MS/TP and takes effect after a power cycle."
    ],
    "gotchas": [
      "Z3-05 defaults to Alarm Only, so the unit keeps running when BACnet traffic stops.",
      "Z3-13 settings 2 and 3 let the bypass restart from stored BACnet commands at power-up before any new message arrives.",
      "BV56 Parameter Enter writes EEPROM; don't use it cyclically.",
      "BV72-BV79 do nothing unless Z3-12 = 1, and then they are ORed with the hard-wired inputs.",
      "Frequency objects use the o1-03 display units."
    ]
  },
